.TH GIT-CLK 1 "2026-09-22" "git-clk" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-clk \- Enhanced git log and statistics reporting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git clk
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ --
.IR git-log-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-clk
provides enhanced git logging and statistics reporting with multiple output styles and convenient filtering options. It simplifies common git log operations with pre-configured formats and cumulative change statistics.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B log
Display a pretty one-line formatted git log with color and optional graph views. Supports multiple output styles.
.TP
.B stats
Show cumulative change statistics including commits, files changed, lines added/deleted, and add/delete ratio. Defaults to filtering by the current user.
.TP
.B my-branches
List all branches on the remote that belong to you (filtered by
.BR git\ config\ user.name ).
.SH COMPATIBILITY ALIASES
The following commands are provided for backward compatibility with existing aliases:
.TP
.B glog
Equivalent to
.BR "log --style=pretty" .
.TP
.B glog1
Equivalent to
.BR "log --style=tree --all" .
.TP
.B glog2
Equivalent to
.BR "log --style=tree2" .
.TP
.B report1
Equivalent to
.BR "stats --me" .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options apply to both
.B log
and
.B stats
commands:
.TP
.BR -g ", " --reflog
Use reflog walk (equivalent to
.BR "git log -g" ).
.TP
.BR -a ", " --all
Include all refs (equivalent to
.BR "git log --all" ).
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help message.
.SH LOG OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --style= STYLE
Select output style. Valid styles:
.RS
.IP \fBpretty\fP
One-line colored format with hash, refs, subject, relative date, and author (default).
.IP \fBtree\fP
Graph view with relative dates, good for viewing branch history.
.IP \fBtree2\fP
Graph view with absolute dates and wrapped subjects for detailed history.
.RE
.SH STATS OPTIONS
.TP
.B --me
Use the author name from
.B git config user.name
(this is the default).
.TP
.BI --author \ PATTERN
Filter by author pattern (passed to
.BR "git log --author=" ).
.TP
.BI --since \ DATE
Show commits since the specified date (passed through to
.BR git\ log ).
.TP
.BI --until \ DATE
Show commits until the specified date (passed through to
.BR git\ log ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Show a pretty one-line log:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk log
.fi
.RE

Show a graph view of all branches:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk log --style=tree --all
.fi
.RE

Show statistics for your commits in the last week:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk stats --since="1 week ago"
.fi
.RE

Show statistics for a specific author:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk stats --author="John Doe"
.fi
.RE

Pass additional git log options after
.BR -- :
.RS
.nf
$ git clk log --style=tree -- --max-count=20
$ git clk stats -- --since="2026-01-01"
.fi
.RE

Show your branches on the remote:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk my-branches
.fi
.RE

Use reflog to see recent branch switches:
.RS
.nf
$ git clk log --reflog --style=pretty
.fi
.RE
.SH STATISTICS OUTPUT
The
.B stats
command provides the following metrics:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Commits
\- Number of commits by the author
.IP \(bu 2
.B "Files changed (total)"
\- Total file entries across all commits
.IP \(bu 2
.B "Lines added (total)"
\- Total lines inserted
.IP \(bu 2
.B "Lines deleted (total)"
\- Total lines deleted
.IP \(bu 2
.B "Total lines (delta)"
\- Net change (added minus deleted)
.IP \(bu 2
.B "Add./Del. ratio"
\- Ratio of deletions to additions (1:n format)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
All options after
.B --
are passed directly to
.BR git\ log .
.IP \(bu 2
The
.B --reflog
flag is useful for seeing your recent navigation history, not just commits.
.IP \(bu 2
Colors in
.B log
output may not display properly on all terminals.
.IP \(bu 2
The
.B stats
command uses
.B git log --numstat
for reliable parsing of changes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B git-clk
exits with status 0 on success, and non-zero on error (e.g., invalid command, missing author for stats).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-log (1),
.BR git-reflog (1),
.BR git-for-each-ref (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by cking.
